{"v":15,"id":"e06","kid":"emma","title":"Octopuses: Clever Animals of the Sea","zh":"章鱼：海洋里的聪明家伙","level":"B1","genre":"自然","src":"facts","sum":"章鱼有八条腕、三颗心、没有骨头，大部分神经细胞长在腕上。它们会开罐子、会逃跑、会伪装，还会喷墨汁。研究章鱼让我们明白\"聪明\"不止一种。","words":279,"paras":[{"t":"With eight arms, three hearts and no bones, the octopus looks like something from another planet. But this strange animal is one of the smartest creatures in the ocean.","w":[[0,4,"with",-1],[5,10,"eight",-1],[11,15,"arms",-1],[17,22,"three",-1],[23,29,"hearts",-1],[30,33,"and",-1],[34,36,"no",-1],[37,42,"bones",-1],[44,47,"the",-1],[48,55,"octopus",-1],[56,61,"looks",-1],[62,66,"like",-1],[67,76,"something",-1],[77,81,"from",-1],[82,89,"another",-1],[90,96,"planet",-1],[98,101,"but",-1],[102,106,"this",-1],[107,114,"strange",-1],[115,121,"animal",-1],[122,124,"is",-1],[125,128,"one",-1],[129,131,"of",-1],[132,135,"the",-1],[136,144,"smartest",-1],[145,154,"creatures",-1],[155,157,"in",-1],[158,161,"the",-1],[162,167,"ocean",-1]]},{"t":"An octopus has about 500 million nerve cells, far more than most animals without a backbone. Surprisingly, most of these cells are not in its head but in its arms. This means each arm can touch, taste and even \"think\" a little on its own. The suckers on the arms can taste whatever they touch.","w":[[0,2,"an",-1],[3,10,"octopus",-1],[11,14,"has",-1],[15,20,"about",-1],[25,32,"million",-1],[33,38,"nerve",0],[39,44,"cells",0],[46,49,"far",11],[50,54,"more",11],[55,59,"than",11],[60,64,"most",-1],[65,72,"animals",-1],[73,80,"without",-1],[81,82,"a",-1],[83,91,"backbone",-1],[93,105,"surprisingly",-1],[107,111,"most",-1],[112,114,"of",-1],[115,120,"these",-1],[121,126,"cells",-1],[127,130,"are",-1],[131,134,"not",-1],[135,137,"in",-1],[138,141,"its",-1],[142,146,"head",-1],[147,150,"but",-1],[151,153,"in",-1],[154,157,"its",-1],[158,162,"arms",-1],[164,168,"this",-1],[169,174,"means",-1],[175,179,"each",-1],[180,183,"arm",-1],[184,187,"can",-1],[188,193,"touch",-1],[195,200,"taste",-1],[201,204,"and",-1],[205,209,"even",-1],[211,216,"think",-1],[218,219,"a",-1],[220,226,"little",-1],[227,229,"on",1],[230,233,"its",1],[234,237,"own",1],[239,242,"the",-1],[243,250,"suckers",-1],[251,253,"on",-1],[254,257,"the",-1],[258,262,"arms",-1],[263,266,"can",-1],[267,272,"taste",-1],[273,281,"whatever",-1],[282,286,"they",-1],[287,292,"touch",-1]]},{"t":"Octopuses are excellent problem solvers. In aquariums, scientists have watched them unscrew jars to get the food inside. In 2016, news reports around the world told the story of Inky, an octopus who escaped from an aquarium in New Zealand. He squeezed through a small gap in his tank, crossed the floor and slid down a pipe into the sea. In the wild, one kind of octopus collects coconut shells and carries them around as a portable house.","w":[[0,9,"octopuses",-1],[10,13,"are",-1],[14,23,"excellent",-1],[24,31,"problem",2],[32,39,"solvers",2],[41,43,"in",-1],[44,53,"aquariums",-1],[55,65,"scientists",-1],[66,70,"have",-1],[71,78,"watched",-1],[79,83,"them",-1],[84,91,"unscrew",-1],[92,96,"jars",-1],[97,99,"to",-1],[100,103,"get",-1],[104,107,"the",-1],[108,112,"food",-1],[113,119,"inside",-1],[121,123,"in",-1],[130,134,"news",-1],[135,142,"reports",-1],[143,149,"around",-1],[150,153,"the",-1],[154,159,"world",-1],[160,164,"told",-1],[165,168,"the",-1],[169,174,"story",-1],[175,177,"of",-1],[178,182,"Inky",-1],[184,186,"an",-1],[187,194,"octopus",-1],[195,198,"who",-1],[199,206,"escaped",-1],[207,211,"from",-1],[212,214,"an",-1],[215,223,"aquarium",-1],[224,226,"in",-1],[227,230,"new",3],[231,238,"Zealand",3],[240,242,"he",-1],[243,251,"squeezed",-1],[252,259,"through",-1],[260,261,"a",-1],[262,267,"small",-1],[268,271,"gap",-1],[272,274,"in",-1],[275,278,"his",-1],[279,283,"tank",-1],[285,292,"crossed",-1],[293,296,"the",-1],[297,302,"floor",-1],[303,306,"and",-1],[307,311,"slid",-1],[312,316,"down",-1],[317,318,"a",-1],[319,323,"pipe",-1],[324,328,"into",-1],[329,332,"the",-1],[333,336,"sea",-1],[338,340,"in",4],[341,344,"the",4],[345,349,"wild",4],[351,354,"one",-1],[355,359,"kind",-1],[360,362,"of",-1],[363,370,"octopus",-1],[371,379,"collects",-1],[380,387,"coconut",5],[388,394,"shells",5],[395,398,"and",-1],[399,406,"carries",-1],[407,411,"them",-1],[412,418,"around",-1],[419,421,"as",-1],[422,423,"a",-1],[424,432,"portable",-1],[433,438,"house",-1]]},{"t":"Octopuses are also masters of disguise. Special cells in their skin let them change color in less than a second. They can even change the texture of their skin to look like rocks, sand or seaweed. If a hungry shark does find one, the octopus has another trick: it shoots out a cloud of dark ink and quickly swims away.","w":[[0,9,"octopuses",-1],[10,13,"are",-1],[14,18,"also",-1],[19,26,"masters",6],[27,29,"of",6],[30,38,"disguise",6],[40,47,"special",-1],[48,53,"cells",-1],[54,56,"in",-1],[57,62,"their",-1],[63,67,"skin",-1],[68,71,"let",-1],[72,76,"them",-1],[77,83,"change",-1],[84,89,"color",-1],[90,92,"in",-1],[93,97,"less",7],[98,102,"than",7],[103,104,"a",-1],[105,111,"second",-1],[113,117,"they",-1],[118,121,"can",-1],[122,126,"even",-1],[127,133,"change",-1],[134,137,"the",-1],[138,145,"texture",-1],[146,148,"of",-1],[149,154,"their",-1],[155,159,"skin",-1],[160,162,"to",-1],[163,167,"look",-1],[168,172,"like",-1],[173,178,"rocks",-1],[180,184,"sand",-1],[185,187,"or",-1],[188,195,"seaweed",-1],[197,199,"if",-1],[200,201,"a",-1],[202,208,"hungry",-1],[209,214,"shark",-1],[215,219,"does",-1],[220,224,"find",-1],[225,228,"one",-1],[230,233,"the",-1],[234,241,"octopus",-1],[242,245,"has",-1],[246,253,"another",-1],[254,259,"trick",-1],[261,263,"it",-1],[264,270,"shoots",8],[271,274,"out",8],[275,276,"a",-1],[277,282,"cloud",-1],[283,285,"of",-1],[286,290,"dark",-1],[291,294,"ink",-1],[295,298,"and",-1],[299,306,"quickly",-1],[307,312,"swims",-1],[313,317,"away",-1]]},{"t":"Strangely, these clever animals have short lives. Most kinds live only one or two years. A mother octopus guards her eggs for weeks or even months without eating.","w":[[0,9,"strangely",-1],[11,16,"these",-1],[17,23,"clever",-1],[24,31,"animals",-1],[32,36,"have",-1],[37,42,"short",-1],[43,48,"lives",-1],[50,54,"most",-1],[55,60,"kinds",-1],[61,65,"live",-1],[66,70,"only",-1],[71,74,"one",-1],[75,77,"or",-1],[78,81,"two",-1],[82,87,"years",-1],[89,90,"a",-1],[91,97,"mother",-1],[98,105,"octopus",-1],[106,112,"guards",-1],[113,116,"her",-1],[117,121,"eggs",-1],[122,125,"for",-1],[126,131,"weeks",-1],[132,134,"or",-1],[135,139,"even",-1],[140,146,"months",-1],[147,154,"without",-1],[155,161,"eating",-1]]},{"t":"Scientists are still learning about how octopuses think. Because their brains are so different from ours, studying them helps us understand that there is more than one way to be smart.","w":[[0,10,"scientists",-1],[11,14,"are",-1],[15,20,"still",-1],[21,29,"learning",-1],[30,35,"about#2",-1],[36,39,"how",-1],[40,49,"octopuses",-1],[50,55,"think",-1],[57,64,"because",-1],[65,70,"their",-1],[71,77,"brains",-1],[78,81,"are",-1],[82,84,"so",-1],[85,94,"different",10],[95,99,"from",10],[100,104,"ours",-1],[106,114,"studying",-1],[115,119,"them",-1],[120,125,"helps",-1],[126,128,"us",-1],[129,139,"understand",-1],[140,144,"that",-1],[145,150,"there",-1],[151,153,"is",-1],[154,158,"more",9],[159,163,"than",9],[164,167,"one",9],[168,171,"way",9],[172,174,"to",-1],[175,177,"be",-1],[178,183,"smart",-1]]}],"gl":{"with":["with","/wɪð/","prep. 和……一起；用","override"],"eight":["eight","/eɪt/","num. 八，八个","level"],"arms":["arms","/ɑrmz/","（章鱼的）腕；手臂","hand"],"three":["three","/θri/","num. 三","override"],"hearts":["heart","/hɑrts/","n. 心脏","level"],"and":["and","/ənd/","conj. 和","level"],"no":["no","/noʊ/","det. 没有","override"],"bones":["bone","/boʊnz/","骨头","level"],"the":["the","/ðə/","art. 这个，那个（特指）","override"],"octopus":["octopus","/ˈɑktəpʊs/","n. 章鱼","ecdict"],"looks":["look","/lʊks/","v. 看；看起来","override"],"like":["like","/laɪk/","prep. 像","override"],"something":["something","/ˈsʌmθɪŋ/","pron. 某事，某物","level"],"from":["fr